==English==
{{was wotd|2025|January|13}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*grewbʰ-}}
From {{compound|en|bumper|t1=(''noun'') thing which is particularly abundant, excellent, or large; (''adjective'') particularly abundant, excellent, or large|crop|notext=1|type=endocentric}}, originally referring to a very large harvest of a crop.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbʌmpə ˌkɹɒp/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bumper crop.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbʌmpəɹ ˌkɹɑp/|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|bump|er crop}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} An [[excess#Noun|excess]] of something; a [[large#Adjective|large]] [[yield#Noun|yield]].
#: {{ux|en|The kindergarten seems to have a '''bumper crop''' of new children this year.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=11 Feb 91|volume=18|number=29|journal=Gay Community News|page=10|title=My Life As A Queer|author=Eric R. Rofes|text=And then the Gay Rights Movement took over and I watched a new generation of homos coming down the assembly line. The Anita Bryant and John Briggs madness of the late '70s brought a '''bumper crop''' of new activists onto the scene who were different than the Gay Lib queers.}}

